  "note": "e2e fixture for #892: the radial in/out flight markers used to be placed from the hull's position in its OWN frame, which inside a #850 building bubble is its offset from a DECK, not the line to the planet. No shipped pad can show that: the only spawnable bubble bed (res/data/ksp_launch_sites.json's kerbin_dock) parks the hull 50 m along the dock's own Z, which is the local vertical, so the buggy and fixed directions agree to 1e-4 rad there (measured, tmp/night3/892_dock_probe.log), and kerbin_station -- which does spin -- spins about its own up axis, which leaves the planet straight under the deck, and carries no VAB_LAUNCH_PAD anyway. So this fixture authors the discriminating state: kerbin_spin_pad, an ORBITAL VAB_LAUNCH_PAD on the shipped dock's 300 km shell whose bubble tips about a LOCAL X axis at 2 deg/s. The deck turns under a hull that rides it, so the direction to Kerbin sweeps 2 deg/s through the bubble axes while the deck's own normal does not -- which is the whole difference between pointing at the planet and pointing at the floor. Bodies are 883-twin-stations.json's Kerbol and Kerbin verbatim (its Moho and Duna are dropped: nothing here leaves Kerbin's SOI); main_space_port stays so Kerbin keeps a default ground pad. Pinned by e2e/cases/render/892-radial-pair-in-a-tipping-bubble.txt."
